      "source": [
        "## 3. Hypothesis Testing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "\n",
        "alpha = 0.05\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Hypothesis Test 1: Domestic vs International Passengers\")\n",
        "print(\"H0: Mean domestic passengers = Mean international passengers\")\n",
        "print(\"H1: Mean domestic passengers ≠ Mean international passengers\")\n",
        "print(\"Significance level: α = 0.05\")\n",
        "\n",
        "t_stat, p_value = stats.ttest_ind(df[\"Dom_Pax\"], df[\"Int_Pax\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nResults:\")\n",
        "print(f\"T-statistic: {t_stat:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"P-value: {p_value:.6f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Mean Domestic Passengers: {df['Dom_Pax'].mean():.0f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Mean International Passengers: {df['Int_Pax'].mean():.0f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if p_value < alpha:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nConclusion: Reject H0 (p < {alpha})\")\n",
        "    print(\"There is a statistically significant difference between mean domestic passengers and mean international passengers.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nConclusion: Fail to reject H0 (p >= {alpha})\")\n",
        "    print(\"There is not enough evidence to say that mean domestic passengers and mean international passengers are different.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nHypothesis Test 2: Correlation between Total Passengers and Total Flights\")\n",
        "print(\"H0: There is no correlation between total passengers and total flights (ρ = 0)\")\n",
        "print(\"H1: There is a correlation between total passengers and total flights (ρ ≠ 0)\")\n",
        "print(\"Significance level: α = 0.05\")\n",
        "\n",
        "correlation_coef, p_value_corr = stats.pearsonr(df[\"Pax\"], df[\"Flt\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"\\nResults:\")\n",
        "print(f\"Correlation coefficient: {correlation_coef:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"P-value: {p_value_corr:.6f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if p_value_corr < alpha:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nConclusion: Reject H0 (p < {alpha})\")\n",
        "    print(\"There is a statistically significant correlation between total passengers and total flights.\")\n",
        "    if correlation_coef > 0:\n",
        "        print(\"The correlation is positive, meaning that as total flights increase, total passengers also tend to increase.\")\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(\"The correlation is negative, meaning that as total flights increase, total passengers tend to decrease.\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(f\"\\nConclusion: Fail to reject H0 (p >= {alpha})\")\n",
        "    print(\"There is not enough evidence to say there is a significant correlation between total passengers and total flights.\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "x3p1VhkJd4dv"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Hypothesis Test 1 compared the mean number of domestic passengers and international passengers. The mean domestic passenger count was 175,331, while the mean international passenger count was 126,924. The p-value was less than 0.05, so we reject the null hypothesis. This means there is a statistically significant difference between domestic and international passenger averages in this dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "Hypothesis Test 2 tested whether total passengers and total flights are significantly correlated. The correlation coefficient was 0.6592, which shows a moderate-to-strong positive relationship. The p-value was less than 0.05, so we reject the null hypothesis. This means there is a statistically significant positive correlation between total flights and total passengers. In practical terms, as the number of flights increases, total passenger volume also tends to increase."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rdI0jIgqe_7m"
      }
    },
