    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The simple linear regression model used total flights (Flt) to predict total passengers (Pax). The model had an R² score of 0.2977, meaning it explained about 29.8% of the variation in passenger totals. The RMSE was about 46,280 passengers and the MAE was about 36,607 passengers, showing that the model has a moderate amount of prediction error.\n",
        "\n",
        "The model equation is:\n",
        "\n",
        "Predicted Pax = 37,484.48 + 11.45 × Flt\n",
        "\n",
        "This means that for each additional flight, the model predicts approximately 11.45 additional passengers. However, because the R² score is relatively low, total flights alone is not enough to accurately predict total passenger volume."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "w91smy9GfLQj"
      }
    },
