    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The multiple linear regression model used Dom_Pax, Int_Pax, Dom_Flt, Int_Flt, and Dom_RPM to predict total passengers (Pax). The model performed extremely well, with an R² score very close to 1.0, RMSE of about 0.51, and MAE of about 0.49. This means the model’s predictions were almost identical to the actual values.\n",
        "\n",
        "However, this very high performance should be interpreted carefully. Pax is calculated from Dom_Pax and Int_Pax, so the model is using variables that directly make up the target variable. This creates a data leakage issue and explains why the model performs almost perfectly.\n",
        "\n",
        "Because the features were scaled using StandardScaler, the coefficients are based on standardized feature values rather than the original units."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "x4LzubK5fjbq"
      }
    },
